    "anchor": "PBPS arXiv:2609.06905v1 Section2.2 actual reflected conditional law and AppendixC.1 compact-gradient density/closedness analytic prerequisite; SPHMC arXiv:2609.06906v1 Section4.1 covariance-upper/BL dependency only. This authored compact-Schwartz-Sobolev prerequisite is not a quoted numbered source theorem.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. v and F are real pointwise functions with genuine global volume MemLp2; K is compact and tsupport v and tsupport F are contained in K.\nFor every real C2 compact phi, v*Delta phi and F*phi are integrable for volume and integral v*Delta phi=integral F*phi. This generic analytic interface is consumed with these inputs actually derived by the same-D localized resolvent; no all-Schwartz, TD equation or final Sobolev certificate is supplied.\nAll rough functions/class representatives are differentiated only as distributions. Complex test derivatives are real Frechet derivatives on E, real/imaginary projections are real-linear CLMs, and the complex TD pairing is bilinear integral psi*v without conjugation. No Nontrivial or positive-dimensional assumption is added.\nUnder the exact ordinary-volume global L2/support and real compact-C2 PDE assumptions, Construct actual vc,Fc in complex L2(volume), with vc=volume-a.e. ofReal(v) and Fc=volume-a.e. ofReal(F). For every complex Schwartz psi, both (Delta psi)*ofReal(v) and psi*ofReal(F) are L1 and their integrals equal. For T_v=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc) and T_F=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc), derive Delta T_v=T_F and MemSobolev 2 2 T_v. The latter uses B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T and a genuine complex L2 witness, not a supplied regularity result.\nDerive actual all-complex-Schwartz tested PDE with both products L1, genuine complex volume-L2 classes/AE embeddings, actual TD Laplacian and MemSobolev2 using B2=I-(2pi)^-2 Delta. Genuine conditional same originalD before epsilon/f, one actualu before allC2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. No real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/Bochner, BL/Poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/scales distinct; TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
    "text_sha256": "3bf90bfc09994632b8c9ac8bc2add2ca2ecaf79496016f8bb65c92369f376086"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CompactWeakPoissonSobolev.compact_weak_poisson_sobolev",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/FunctionalInequalities/CompactWeakPoissonSobolev.lean",
    "statement": "(v F : E → ℝ) (K : Set E)\n    (hK : IsCompact K) (hv : tsupport v ⊆ K) (hF : tsupport F ⊆ K)\n    (hv2 : MemLp v 2 volume) (hF2 : MemLp F 2 volume)\n    (hweak : ∀ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 2 φ → HasCompactSupport φ →\n      Integrable (fun x => v x * (Δ φ) x) volume ∧\n      Integrable (fun x => F x * φ x) volume ∧\n      (∫ x, v x * (Δ φ) x) = ∫ x, F x * φ x) :\n    ∃ vc Fc : Lp ℂ 2 (volume : Measure E),\n      vc =ᵐ[volume] (fun x => (v x : ℂ)) ∧\n      Fc =ᵐ[volume] (fun x => (F x : ℂ)) ∧\n      (∀ ψ : SchwartzMap E ℂ,\n        Integrable (fun x => (Δ ψ) x * (v x : ℂ)) volume ∧\n        Integrable (fun x => ψ x * (F x : ℂ)) volume ∧\n        (∫ x, (Δ ψ) x * (v x : ℂ)) = ∫ x, ψ x * (F x : ℂ)) ∧\n      Δ (Lp.toTemperedDistribution vc) = Lp.toTemperedDistribution Fc ∧\n      MemSobolev 2 2 (Lp.toTemperedDistribution vc)",
    "statement_sha256": "66a8eb576547ad7100dbff6f80e9d4e64ae69940d4d05f6cea3c90a670fe414f",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is finite-dimensional real Hilbert with Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. All section instances remain part of the contract. NNReal denotes nonnegative real scalars.",
      "MemLp f2volume means actual volume-a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm. Lp F2mu is the genuine L2 quotient with selected standard measurable representative; the statement explicitly binds vc/Fc to the real pointwise inputs via volume-AE ofReal identities. No support equality of selected complex quotient representatives is asserted.",
      "SchwartzMap E complex is the genuine smooth rapidly decreasing test function on real E. Its derivatives are real Frechet derivatives. Laplacian.laplacian is the actual finite-basis trace on smooth test functions, and the true distribution Laplacian on tempered distributions. The rough scalar v/u is not given pointwise classical derivatives.",
      "Lp.toTemperedDistribution at exponent2 and volume is the genuine complex tempered distribution embedding, evaluated on psi by integral psi(x)*vc(x), with no complex conjugation. Real/imaginary CLMs are real-linear; the LpTD and multiplier linearity are complex-linear.",
      "MemSobolev s p T means an actual Lp(volume) witness fprime with besselPotential E complex s T=LpTD(fprime). besselPotential is Fourier multiplier (1+norm(x)^2)^(s/2). The fixed Fourier convention yields Delta T=-(2pi)^2 FM(norm^2)T. Order2 membership here is this exact Bessel-Sobolev statement, not an asserted real Hessian representative or weighted-core theorem.",
      "LinearPMap is the original real-linear partial gradient on a submodule domain; D.graph is actual graph, D.IsClosable its single-valued graph closure and D.closure that same closed operator. The source D is fixed before epsilon/f; u before all chi; complex classes after each chi and before all Schwartz psi.",
      "Measure.tilted h is exp(h)/integral exp(h) times the original measure, requiring the stated integrability/positive normalization facts; Kernel IsMarkovKernel and IsCondKernel denote actual measurable probability transition and joint disintegration, Measure.map/prod actual pushforward/product and stdGaussian the genuine standard finite real Hilbert Gaussian. ContDiff1/2/infinity and compact topological support have their usual exact Lean meanings."
    ],
