  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. All approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. Let v,F:E->R and K a subset of E. Assume K is compact, tsupport(v) is contained in K and tsupport(F) is contained in K. Assume both v and F satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to volume, including volume-a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm.\nAssume that for every real C2 compactly supported phi:E->R, both functions x->v(x)*Delta(phi)(x) and x->F(x)*phi(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral v(x)*Delta(phi)(x) dx = integral F(x)*phi(x) dx.\nHere Delta(phi) is the actual test-function finite-basis Laplacian. No classical derivatives of v or F are assumed.\nThen there exist vc,Fc in Lp C 2 volume such that vc=(x->(v(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere and Fc=(x->(F(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere. For these same vc,Fc all of the following conclusions hold simultaneously:\n(1) For every psi in SchwartzMap E C, both x->Delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):C) and x->psi(x)*(F(x):C) are volume-integrable and\n  integral Delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):C) dx = integral psi(x)*(F(x):C) dx.\n(2) Delta(Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)) = Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc).\n(3) MemSobolev 2 2 (Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)).\nThe classes are selected before all Schwartz tests and the complex test integrals use the original pointwise v and F casts, not newly selected functions per test. The real weak PDE and its two L1 products are premises; the two complex Schwartz L1 products, the complex test equation, the genuine distribution equation and Sobolev membership are conclusions.\nLp C 2 volume is the genuine complex L2 quotient with its standard measurable representative. These volume-a.e. identities bind the chosen classes to the actual pointwise real functions cast into C; they do not assert pointwise support identities for the chosen complex representatives. Every Schwartz test is a genuine smooth rapidly decreasing complex function on the real space E, and no compact-support restriction is imposed on it. Its derivatives are real Frechet derivatives. Pairings and displayed integrals use ordinary complex multiplication with no complex conjugation. Lp.toTemperedDistribution is the genuine complex-linear distribution embedding whose value at psi is integral psi(x)*the L2 representative(x) dx. The distribution Laplacian is the true tempered-distribution operator. MemSobolev 2 2 means there exists an actual fprime in Lp C 2 volume with besselPotential E C 2 of the displayed distribution equal to Lp.toTemperedDistribution(fprime); its multiplier is (1+||xi||^2)^(2/2). The approved Fourier convention is Delta T=-(2*pi)^2 FM(||xi||^2)T. This order-2 Bessel-Sobolev assertion is not a pointwise classical Laplacian, a real Hessian representative, or a weighted-core conclusion.",
